MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink bundle feels like a natural next choice because I already have a Blink camera and could use coverage at the front door and in additional areas.",
    "The Ring floodlight camera matches my interest in outdoor monitoring, while the Echo Show could be useful if it works with my cameras. Both have a possible purpose beyond simply adding another device."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV Stick feels redundant because I already have a 4K stick and a Fire TV television; a themed remote cover gives me no practical reason to add it.",
    "The Echo speakers, car assistant, tablet, and lighting bundle introduce uses I have not been looking for. Sharing Alexa or Amazon branding does not make them useful additions to my video and security setup."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV and Blink purchases seem to have been taken as interest in almost any Amazon or Alexa device.",
    "My interest in connected home equipment seems to have been stretched into interest in speakers and lighting, even though my purchases have clearer viewing and monitoring purposes."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What I already own matters: expanding camera coverage could add value, while another streaming stick would largely repeat an existing function.",
    "Compatibility and a specific need determine whether I would choose something now. I would favor a Blink expansion over another camera system, check camera support before choosing a display, and buy an HDMI cable only when I need one."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in home video and security but treated it too broadly as a desire for more Amazon and Alexa devices."
}
